<blockquote>
<p>A bit odd, since kidneys are not living per say. Perhaps they can be functional or not decaying, but organs of living things are usually not alive themselves.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think it's more that you don't usually see the terms because it's an unusual situation for an organ to be alive separate from the rest of the organism. When you have organ being used for a transplant, though, the organ can be referred to as alive so long as it is viable, and if a living person has necrotic tissue, that tissue is dead even though the person is not.</p>
<p>Regardless, really glad to see this back up. ^_^</p>

